---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About SAICA-Bench.">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl">
    SAICA-Bench tests whether supervision tools catch typical failures of AI coding agents: fabricated code, test
    manipulation, obsolescence, scope creep and more. It compares free programs (type checkers, linters), AI code
    reviewers, evaluation frameworks and plain models on the same samples, with cost.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl">
    Data comes from public datasets with confirmed labels:
    <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/microsoft/delulu" rel="noopener">Delulu</a> (fabricated code) and
    <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/PatronusAI/trace-dataset" rel="noopener">Patronus TRACE</a> (test
    manipulation). The failure-mode taxonomy and tool list come from our knowledge graph of supervision tools
    (<a href="/graph">graph</a>). Code and results are on
    <a href="https://github.com/vasylrakivnenko/SAICA" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p class="max-w-3xl">
    Questions, corrections or a tool to add: <a href="https://github.com/vasylrakivnenko/SAICA/issues" rel="noopener">open
    an issue</a> or email Vasyl Rakivnenko at <a href="mailto:vasyl@stanford.edu">vasyl@stanford.edu</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
